1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,438
This is VOID.

2
00:00:02,188 --> 00:00:04,368
Give an AI agent real on-chain power,

3
00:00:04,388 --> 00:00:06,700
with a guarantee it can never leave your rules.

4
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:09,500
A smart contract checks every action.

5
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:13,288
Every action passes five gates,

6
00:00:13,308 --> 00:00:14,388
in a fixed order:

7
00:00:14,408 --> 00:00:18,000
expiry, spend cap, whitelist, transaction count,

8
00:00:18,020 --> 00:00:18,970
rate limit.

9
00:00:21,370 --> 00:00:22,695
Let's build a vault.

10
00:00:23,420 --> 00:00:26,787
I set the owner, and the one contract and function the agent may

11
00:00:26,807 --> 00:00:28,970
call, then seal the policy on-chain.

12
00:00:29,620 --> 00:00:31,307
Live, on Base Sepolia.

13
00:00:33,158 --> 00:00:33,845
Sealed.

14
00:00:34,533 --> 00:00:35,745
Five gates armed.

15
00:00:36,495 --> 00:00:38,813
I fund it, and take the session key,

16
00:00:38,833 --> 00:00:39,845
shown once.

17
00:00:41,667 --> 00:00:43,042
Now I'm the agent.

18
00:00:43,767 --> 00:00:45,992
Outside the policy, simulated:

19
00:00:46,017 --> 00:00:47,429
blocked at the whitelist.

20
00:00:48,117 --> 00:00:49,129
Now for real.

21
00:00:50,461 --> 00:00:51,749
Reverted on-chain.

22
00:00:52,386 --> 00:00:54,161
The chain itself refused it.

23
00:00:55,892 --> 00:00:58,380
Same key, doing what the policy allows.

24
00:00:59,105 --> 00:01:00,305
It goes straight through.

25
00:01:01,005 --> 00:01:02,542
No human in the loop.

26
00:01:08,585 --> 00:01:11,885
If anything looks wrong, one owner signature pulls the plug.

27
00:01:17,606 --> 00:01:20,031
Now every action is blocked at the first gate.

28
00:01:22,268 --> 00:01:24,730
And what is left sweeps straight back to the owner.

29
00:01:27,318 --> 00:01:28,368
One more test.

30
00:01:29,080 --> 00:01:30,043
That was me.

31
00:01:30,768 --> 00:01:33,355
So I told a real AI agent it was hijacked,

32
00:01:33,455 --> 00:01:34,680
and to drain a vault.

33
00:01:35,393 --> 00:01:38,148
It tried the whole balance, sneaking under the cap,

34
00:01:38,168 --> 00:01:40,955
a token transfer, even uninstalling the policy.

35
00:01:41,643 --> 00:01:44,005
Five attempts, five rejections.

36
00:01:44,705 --> 00:01:46,643
The one approved action went through.

37
00:01:48,445 --> 00:01:52,175
Real ERC-4337, twenty-eight Foundry tests,

38
00:01:52,195 --> 00:01:53,743
live on Base and Arbitrum.

39
00:01:54,344 --> 00:01:54,919
VOID:

40
00:01:54,945 --> 00:01:58,164
session keys for agents that the contract itself enforces.
